Engine: what the acting unit's weapons can hit now, "CTGT" (open fix 54).

STATUS: APPLIED 30 September 2026 by work order 194 (Part B; reserved by
work order 193) — orion2re 750434ef on orionlayer-local (before: f1e6c581), this
file's diff byte for byte (index lines included). Required by
tools/version_check.py since work order 194.

It was applied, from ~/orion2re on the orionlayer-local branch, with:

    patch -p1 < ~/orionlayerv3/doc/ext_combat_targets.patch

and a rebuild. It comes back off with `git revert 750434ef` or `patch -R -p1`,
and a rebuild.

WHAT IT IS FOR

    Whether a weapon slot can hit a unit or a missile is decided inside
    CMBTFIRE::Fire_Ship_ at the moment of the shot: the target inside the
    slot's arc (Get_Weapon_Arc_ of Relative_Bearing_ / _XY_), ammunition by
    the slot's type (a torpedo fires with ammo 0, anything else needs
    ammo), Weapon_In_Range_ and Target_Is_Legal_For_Weapon_ (cmbtfire.cpp).
    A client that shows legal targets would have to recompute range, arcs
    and every special rule — the kind of copy this project refuses (open
    fix 48 sent the move verdict for the same reason). Block "CTGT", after
    CRES while a battle is live and a unit acts: for the acting unit, one
    byte per unit and one per live missile, bit k = slot k can hit it now.
    Not in it: whether the player has the slot switched on (CMBT's
    `active`) and the reload Fire_Ship_ does on its way (CMBT's shots_left
    and status).

    193 left one question open: whether the two functions have side
    effects. Work order 194 read them and every helper they call —
    Weapon_In_Range_, Target_Is_Legal_For_Weapon_, Weapon_Can_Fire_At_
    Missiles_, Can_Bomb_Planet_, Range_To_Ship_(_Squares_), Range_To_
    Missile_, Range_To_XY_(_With_Offset_), Ship_Center_Offsets_,
    special::Range_, Relative_Bearing_(_XY_), angle::Get_Angle_,
    Get_Weapon_Arc_, Ship_Is_In_Stasis_, Does_Combat_Ship_Have_Special_:
    none writes game state, none draws a random number, none ticks. So an
    engine without OrionLayer behaves exactly as before. One marker,
    `OrionLayer, open fix 54.`, on the block's first comment line.

diff --git a/src/ext/ext_api.cpp b/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
index 37bfd2da..7ea40161 100644
--- a/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
+++ b/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
@@ -1554,6 +1554,68 @@ static void SerializeState(std::vector<uint8_t>& buf,
             Write16(buf, u.structure_max);
         }
     }
+
+    // 22. What the acting unit's weapons can hit now: "CTGT", written ONLY
+    //     while a battle is live and a unit acts, after CRES.
+    //     OrionLayer, open fix 54.
+    //
+    //     The engine's own verdict, as CMBTFIRE::Fire_Ship_ takes it for each
+    //     weapon slot (cmbtfire.cpp): the target inside the slot's arc
+    //     (Get_Weapon_Arc_ of Relative_Bearing_ / _XY_), ammunition by the
+    //     slot's type (a torpedo fires with ammo 0, anything else needs ammo),
+    //     Weapon_In_Range_ and Target_Is_Legal_For_Weapon_. All of them only
+    //     read (work order 194 read each and every helper they call: no write,
+    //     no random number). NOT in it: whether the player has the slot
+    //     switched on (`active`, CMBT has it) and the reload Fire_Ship_ does
+    //     on its way (shots_left / status, CMBT has both). Per unit, then per
+    //     live missile: one byte, bit k = slot k can hit it.
+    if (g_combat_live && MOX::_combat_data != nullptr && MOX::_missile != nullptr &&
+        MOX::_cur_ship >= 0 && MOX::_cur_ship < MOX::_combat_total_ship_count &&
+        MOX::_combat_total_ship_count <= 210) {
+        const int16_t src = MOX::_cur_ship;
+        const int16_t units = MOX::_combat_total_ship_count;
+        buf.push_back((uint8_t)'C');
+        buf.push_back((uint8_t)'T');
+        buf.push_back((uint8_t)'G');
+        buf.push_back((uint8_t)'T');
+        Write8(buf, 1);                                   // block version
+        Write16(buf, (int16_t)g_combat_serial);
+        Write16(buf, src);
+        auto slot_mask = [&](int16_t target, int16_t flag, uint8_t arc) {
+            uint8_t mask = 0;
+            for (int16_t k = 0; k < 8; k++) {
+                const s_combat_weapon_slot& w = MOX::_combat_data[src].weapons[k];
+                if (w.weapon_id == 0 || (arc & w.arc) == 0) continue;
+                const bool torpedo = TECHDATA::_weapons[w.weapon_id].type == WEAPON_TYPE_TORPEDO;
+                if (torpedo ? w.ammo != 0 : w.ammo == 0) continue;
+                if (CMBTFIRE::Weapon_In_Range_(k, src, target, flag, 0) != 0 &&
+                    CMBTFIRE::Target_Is_Legal_For_Weapon_(w.weapon_id, w.specials, target, flag) != 0) {
+                    mask |= (uint8_t)(1u << k);
+                }
+            }
+            return mask;
+        };
+        Write16(buf, units);
+        for (int16_t t = 0; t < units; t++) {
+            uint8_t mask = 0;
+            if (t != src && MOX::_combat_data[t].unit_status == 0 &&
+                (t != 0 || MOX::_cmbt_colony_id != -1)) {
+                mask = slot_mask(t, 0, CMBTDRW1::Get_Weapon_Arc_(CMBTDRW1::Relative_Bearing_(src, t)));
+            }
+            Write8(buf, mask);
+        }
+        int16_t live = 0;
+        for (int i = 0; i < 300; i++) {
+            if (MOX::_missile[i].type > 0) ++live;
+        }
+        Write16(buf, live);
+        for (int16_t m = 0; m < 300; m++) {
+            if (MOX::_missile[m].type <= 0) continue;
+            Write16(buf, m);
+            Write8(buf, slot_mask(m, 1, CMBTDRW1::Get_Weapon_Arc_(CMBTDRW1::Relative_Bearing_XY_(
+                src, MOX::_missile[m].x, MOX::_missile[m].y))));
+        }
+    }
 }
 
